WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.920
Iron Man has his armor, Captain America has
his shield, and Spider-Man has his web-shooters,

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:09.400
but there are few superheroes who are as strongly
identified with their equipment as Thor.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:14.320
For centuries, he's been depicted wielding
the mighty Mjolnir, whose crushing blows resound

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.840
with the sound of thunder across the Nine
Realms.

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:20.720
But in the comics, that’s not the only weapon
that the God of Thunder has wielded against

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:21.780
the forces of evil.

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:26.480
Join us as we take a trip through the Asgardian
armory to rank Thor’s hammers from weakest

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:27.180
to strongest!

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.340
Ultimate Mjolnir I

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:34.270
The original version of Mjolnir that we saw
in the pages of The Ultimates wasn't actually

00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:35.240
Mjolnir at all.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.680
Instead, in keeping with that book's questions
about whether Thor was actually a god or just

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:43.690
some delusional but super-powered Norwegian
gentleman, it was the product of technology,

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:44.680
not magic.

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:48.820
While he would eventually turn out to be the
earthly reincarnation of the God of Thunder,

00:00:48.829 --> 00:00:53.420
Thor's original set of equipment was based
entirely on super-science, with a weather-controlling

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:56.240
costume powered by a battery inside a giant
hammer.

00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:59.160
While it was certainly formidable, it was
far from flawless.

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:03.660
As a weapon made by humans, it lacked both
the sheer power of the magical Mjolnir and

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:06.461
the enchantments that made Thor the only one
able to use it.

00:01:06.461 --> 00:01:11.350
That made it pretty easy for villains to replicate,
including a Soviet super-soldier who paired

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:15.880
his hammer with a similarly powerful sickle,
because comics have never exactly been subtle.

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:17.880
Ultimate Mjolnir II

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:22.380
After spending a few years swinging around
his technological hammer, the Thor of the

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:25.140
Ultimate Universe got his hands on the genuine
article.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:30.119
Like the core universe's version of Mjolnir,
this version granted its wielder incredible

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:34.400
powers, most of which involved the ability
to smash problems into a fine red mist.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:38.760
It did not, however, have the worthiness enchantment
or anything else that could keep bad guys

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:42.660
like the Ultimate Universe’s genocidal version
of Magneto from picking it up.

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:44.940
Needless to say, this caused a lot of problems.

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:50.329
When it found its way to the core Marvel universe,
it was used by Volstagg, one of Thor's closest

00:01:50.329 --> 00:01:51.420
Asgardian allies.

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:56.040
When he hefted it in order to defend his realm,
the noble but definitely past-his-prime warrior

00:01:56.049 --> 00:02:00.560
wasn't just turned into Thor, he was turned
into an incredibly powerful version called

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:01.200
War Thor.

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:05.760
Unfortunately, that transformation also made
him prone to violent rages and when it was

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:08.700
destroyed by Mangog, left Volstagg in a coma.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:12.180
A pretty high price to pay just to use a hammer
that's also an axe.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:13.380
Jarnbjorn

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:17.980
While it's technically not a hammer, Jarnbjorn
definitely deserves a spot on the list.

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:22.579
The Odinson wielded this axe in the days before
he proved his worthiness of Mjolnir, and more

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:24.860
recently, when he found himself unworthy once
again.

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:29.640
While it lacks Mjolnir's ability to channel
lightning, it's still a gigantic magic battleaxe

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:30.730
crafted by the gods.

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:34.580
That alone makes it pretty formidable, and
allows it to live up to the meaning of its

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:35.860
name: the Iron Bear.

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:41.040
It's incredibly sharp, can slash through the
armor of the space gods known as the Celestials,

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:45.300
and was also enchanted to be at least as indestructible
as the original Mjolnir.

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:50.160
It's worth noting that Jarnbjorn's most memorable
powerful moment isn't exactly one of its best.

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:54.100
The first time Thor took it into battle after
losing his hammer, it was taken away from

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:57.240
him by Malekith, who promptly used it to cut
off Thor's arm.

00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:00.719
That's the sort of thing that's going to happen
when you're used to swinging around a weapon

00:03:00.719 --> 00:03:04.810
no one else can lift, but any weapon that
can almost effortlessly sever a god's limbs

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:06.260
has to be pretty potent.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:08.280
The Golden Hammer

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:13.500
After Mjolnir's destruction, Thor contacted
a dwarven blacksmith named Screwbeard, and

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:14.560
got him to make a new hammer.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:18.280
The bad news is that this hammer broke on
its first outing when Thor shattered it by

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:19.860
hitting the unstoppable Juggernaut.

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:24.160
The good news is that Screwbeard had made
plenty of backup hammers, and teleported an

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:25.780
entire arsenal to Thor.

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:28.840
Eventually, he found one that would stand
up to some heavy use.

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:32.930
The Golden Hammer is still new enough that
it hasn't been named yet although Screwbeard

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:37.089
mentioned that one of the other destroyed
hammers was called "Hulksmiter" so it's difficult

00:03:37.089 --> 00:03:38.420
to judge its true power.

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:42.180
It has, however, been mentioned in the comics
that it's made of a less pure form of the

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:46.440
metal ore Uru, and likely won't hold up as
well as the original Mjolnir did.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:48.460
Mjolnir

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:53.260
The original Mjolnir has long been considered
one of the Marvel Universe's most powerful

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:54.780
artifacts, and for good reason.

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:59.260
Even if it was just an indestructible uru
mallet empowered by the Odinforce, it would

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:03.200
be a pretty respectable weapon, but that's
just the tip of this particular enchanted

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:03.700
iceberg.

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:08.360
What really makes Mjolnir so powerful is that
it's directly tied into the power and godhood

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:08.980
of Thor.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:13.080
The enchantment on the hammer means that anyone
worthy enough can truly become the God of

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:17.720
Thunder by lifting it, including Jane Foster,
Beta Ray Bill, and even Loki.

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:22.620
But while Mjolnir weathered plenty of figurative
and literal storms in its time, Odin probably

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:24.540
should've asked about a lifetime warranty.

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:29.280
In the movies, Hela crushed it into bits,
and in the comics, it was destroyed when Thor

00:04:29.289 --> 00:04:33.919
Jane Foster took it into battle against the
otherwise unstoppable Mangog, launching it

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:35.140
and the villain into the sun.

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:39.639
The only thing that survived was a pebble-sized
chunk of Uru that was still pretty difficult

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:40.840
for the unworthy to lift.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:45.300
Still, you have to give it credit: a hammer
that can only be destroyed by something that's

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:50.120
27,000,000 degrees Fahrenheit and constantly
exploding with nuclear reactions isn't exactly

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:50.740
fragile.

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:52.540
Stormbreaker

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:57.800
In the movies, Stormbreaker is Thor’s devastating
new Groot-handled hammer, but in the comics,

00:04:57.800 --> 00:04:59.360
it belongs to Beta Ray Bill.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:03.639
He’s an alien hero who once found himself
battling Thor, and during the fight, he was

00:05:03.639 --> 00:05:07.830
able to prove his worthiness by lifting the
hammer and briefly taking over the identity

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:08.460
of Thor.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:12.540
After Odin decreed that the two heroes would
battle to the death to determine who would

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:17.300
get the hammer and the title a battle that
Bill actually won Bill once again proved himself

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:21.400
by saving Thor's life, and swore an oath to
be an ally and "oath-brother."

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:26.220
To reward his valor and cement the alliance,
Odin granted him Stormbreaker, a new golden

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:28.940
hammer said to be Mjolnir's equal in every
way.

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:31.860
So if they're equals, why does Stormbreaker
rank higher?

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:35.310
Simple: Mjolnir got destroyed, but Stormbreaker's
still around.

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:37.529
Being in one piece tends to give it a bit
of an edge.

